      "message": "feat(mcp): pick faces, edge chains and loops for an operation's area\n\nFour MCP tools so an agent can choose what an operation machines:\n\n- list_features: a model's planar faces (each boundary loop with the\n  tangent edge chains that run it), edge chains, welded smooth faces\n  and corner vertices, under their stable geometry-hash ids, written\n  as \"<kind>:0x<hex>\" strings (a JSON number cannot carry a 64-bit\n  hash exactly through every client).\n- set_operation_geometry: the op's source becomes the picked features\n  through SetOperationGeometry - one undo step, so undo restores the\n  previous source. A loop is picked by the chains list_features names\n  for it.\n- get_operation_geometry: source, picks, area controls and the\n  selection notes.\n- set_operation_area: the area controls through\n  EditOperationParams::with_area, one undo step.\n\nRefusals are tool errors: malformed or unknown ids, a non-model, an\nempty pick list, and a feature kind the op cannot take (a vertex for a\nkind whose picks author its region, anything but a chain for\nMulti-Axis Contour - generation's own refusals, said at the pick;\nselection_drives_region becomes pub(crate) for it). Everything else is\nthe commands' own doors.\n\nThe handlers live in new modules (mcp/features.rs, pick.rs, area.rs);\ntools.rs and mod.rs only gain the registration lines. Pinned by the new\nmcp_pick suite: a pocket's floor loop picked off an imported STL,\ngenerated, verified and posted inside the ring down to the floor, the\narea set and undone, the pick undone back to the model source.\n\nFixes #180\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
